course: dictionary
lesson: 14177
title: Big words for big moments
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how important something is. Momentous is one of them. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The Moon landing was a momentous event.» A landing on the Moon is a huge thing, so momentous must mean very important.
explain: Clues often come from what happens next. «Tom had to choose: stay in his village or move to the city. It was a momentous decision.» A choice that decides where you will live for years must be a big one, so momentous means it will change things a lot.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «It was a very important decision» and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Momentous means very important, with big effects on the future.
fact: «Momentous» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «a momentous event» or «a momentous day».
fact: History lessons often use momentous for great events, such as «the Moon landing».
fact: In stories, a momentous moment is often a big decision, when a character's life is about to change.
fact: Do not confuse momentous with momentary, which means lasting only a very short time.
exercise: «The Moon landing was a momentous event.» What does momentous mean? | Funny and silly | Very quiet and small | Happening every single day | *Very important, with big effects on the future
exercise: «Leaving his village was a momentous decision for Tom.» What does this tell us? | *The choice will change his life a lot in the future | Tom did not mind at all | Tom had a nice lunch before he left | The village was very small
exercise: «The king signed the law, and it was a momentous day for the whole country.» Find and copy one word that means very important. | country | king | *momentous | signed
test: Which event is most likely to be momentous? | Eating toast for breakfast | A bus arriving on time | A cat sleeping in the sun | *The first person to walk on the Moon
test: Ella says, «Moving house is momentous for us.» What does she mean? | *The move will change our lives a lot | We will move in one minute | The new house is very dark | It is a small matter, not worth noticing
exam: Dad says, «Signing this deal is a momentous step.» What does momentous mean? | Very quiet and gentle | *Very important, with big effects on the future | Easy to do and quickly forgotten | Left over and not needed
